","Modernes KI-Tool"],"pt":["Construída com Vue 3 + Vite + TypeScript","Ferramenta de colagem de fotos moderna","Código aberto","Ideal para desenvolvedores","Fácil de usar"],"ru":["Построен на Vue 3 + Vite + TypeScript","Современный инструмент для создания коллажей","Открытый исходный код","Идеален для разработчиков","Легко использовать"],"ar":["مبنية على Vue 3 + Vite + TypeScript","أداة 콜اج الصور الحديثة","مفتوح المصدر","مثالية للمطورين","سهل الاستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["json-canvas","AI工具","照片拼接","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","如何使用json-canvas","json-canvas安装","json-canvas教程"],"ja":["json-canvas","AIエージェント","写真パッチ","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","json-canvasの使い方","json-canvasのインストール","json-canvasのチュートリアル"],"ko":["json-canvas","AI 에이전트","사진拼接","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","json-canvas 사용법","json-canvas 설치","json-canvas 튜토리얼"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","json-canvas","collage de fotos","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","cómo usar json-canvas","alternativas a json-canvas"],"fr":["outils d''IA","json-canvas","collage de photos","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","comment utiliser json-canvas","alternatives à json-canvas"],"de":["KI-Tools","json-canvas","Foto-Collage","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","wie man json-canvas verwendet","Alternativen zu json-canvas"],"pt":["json-canvas","ferramenta de colagem de fotos","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","código aberto","desenvolvedores","como usar json-canvas","json-canvas alternative"],"ru":["json-canvas","ИИ Агенты","инструмент для создания коллажей","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","открытый исходный код","разработчики","как использовать json-canvas","json-canvas vs конкуренты"],"ar":["json-canvas","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","أداة 콜اج الصور","Vue 3","Vite","TypeScript","مفتوح المصدر","مطورين","كيفية استخدام json-canvas","json-canvas بديل"]}},"owner":"hviwen","repo":"mosaic-photo","repoPath":"hviwen/mosaic-photo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.967Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"json-canvas","description":"Create and edit JSON Canvas files (.canvas) with nodes, edges, groups, and connections. Use when working with .canvas files, creating visual canvases, mind maps, flowcharts, or when the user mentions Canvas files in Obsidian.","bodyPreview":"# JSON Canvas Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid JSON Canvas files (`.canvas`) used in Obsidian and other applications.\n\n## Overview\n\nJSON Canvas is an open file format for infinite canvas data. Canvas files use the `.canvas` extension and contain valid JSON following the [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/).\n\n## File Structure\n\nA canvas file contains two top-level arrays:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n- `nodes` (optio","body":"# JSON Canvas Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid JSON Canvas files (`.canvas`) used in Obsidian and other applications.\n\n## Overview\n\nJSON Canvas is an open file format for infinite canvas data. Canvas files use the `.canvas` extension and contain valid JSON following the [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/).\n\n## File Structure\n\nA canvas file contains two top-level arrays:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n- `nodes` (optional): Array of node objects\n- `edges` (optional): Array of edge objects connecting nodes\n\n## Nodes\n\nNodes are objects placed on the canvas. There are four node types:\n- `text` - Text content with Markdown\n- `file` - Reference to files/attachments\n- `link` - External URL\n- `group` - Visual container for other nodes\n\n### Z-Index Ordering\n\nNodes are ordered by z-index in the array:\n- First node = bottom layer (displayed below others)\n- Last node = top layer (displayed above others)\n\n### Generic Node Attributes\n\nAll nodes share these attributes:\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | Yes | string | Unique identifier for the node |\n| `type` | Yes | string | Node type: `text`, `file`, `link`, or `group` |\n| `x` | Yes | integer | X position in pixels |\n| `y` | Yes | integer | Y position in pixels |\n| `width` | Yes | integer | Width in pixels |\n| `height` | Yes | integer | Height in pixels |\n| `color` | No | canvasColor | Node color (see Color section) |\n\n### Text Nodes\n\nText nodes contain Markdown content.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"x\": 0,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 200,\n  \"text\": \"# Hello World\\n\\nThis is **Markdown** content.\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Newline Escaping (Common Pitfall)\n\nIn JSON, newline characters inside strings **must** be represented as `\\n`. Do **not** use the literal sequence `\\\\n` in a `.canvas` file—Obsidian will render it as the characters `\\` and `n` instead of a line break.\n\nExamples:\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Line 1\\nLine 2\" }\n```\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Line 1\\\\nLine 2\" }\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | Yes | string | Plain text with Markdown syntax |\n\n### File Nodes\n\nFile nodes reference files or attachments (images, videos, PDFs, notes, etc.).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f67890\",\n  \"type\": \"file\",\n  \"x\": 500,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 300,\n  \"file\": \"Attachments/diagram.png\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"b2c3d4e5f6789012\",\n  \"type\": \"file\",\n  \"x\": 500,\n  \"y\": 400,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 300,\n  \"file\": \"Notes/Project Overview.md\",\n  \"subpath\": \"#Implementation\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `file` | Yes | string | Path to file within the system |\n| `subpath` | No | string | Link to heading or block (starts with `#`) |\n\n### Link Nodes\n\nLink nodes display external URLs.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"c3d4e5f678901234\",\n  \"type\": \"link\",\n  \"x\": 1000,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 200,\n  \"url\": \"https://obsidian.md\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `url` | Yes | string | External URL |\n\n### Group Nodes\n\nGroup nodes are visual containers for organizing other nodes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"d4e5f6789012345a\",\n  \"type\": \"group\",\n  \"x\": -50,\n  \"y\": -50,\n  \"width\": 1000,\n  \"height\": 600,\n  \"label\": \"Project Overview\",\n  \"color\": \"4\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"e5f67890123456ab\",\n  \"type\": \"group\",\n  \"x\": 0,\n  \"y\": 700,\n  \"width\": 800,\n  \"height\": 500,\n  \"label\": \"Resources\",\n  \"background\": \"Attachments/background.png\",\n  \"backgroundStyle\": \"cover\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `label` | No | string | Text label for the group |\n| `background` | No | string | Path to background image |\n| `backgroundStyle` | No | string | Background rendering style |\n\n#### Background Styles\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `cover` | Fills entire width and height of node |\n| `ratio` | Maintains aspect ratio of background image |\n| `repeat` | Repeats image as pattern in both directions |\n\n## Edges\n\nEdges are lines connecting nodes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"f67890123456789a\",\n  \"fromNode\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"toNode\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f67890\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"0123456789abcdef\",\n  \"fromNode\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n  \"fromEnd\": \"none\",\n  \"toNode\": \"b2c3d4e5f6789012\",\n  \"toSide\": \"left\",\n  \"toEnd\": \"arrow\",\n  \"color\": \"1\",\n  \"label\": \"leads to\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `id` | Yes | string | - | Unique identifier for the edge |\n| `fromNode` | Yes | string | - | Node ID where connection starts |\n| `fromSide` | No | string | - | Side where edge starts |\n| `fromEnd` | No | string | `none` | Shape at edge start |\n| `toNode` | Yes | string | - | Node ID where connection ends |\n| `toSide` | No | string | - | Side where edge ends |\n| `toEnd` | No | string | `arrow` | Shape at edge end |\n| `color` | No | canvasColor | - | Line color |\n| `label` | No | string | - | Text label for the edge |\n\n### Side Values\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `top` | Top edge of node |\n| `right` | Right edge of node |\n| `bottom` | Bottom edge of node |\n| `left` | Left edge of node |\n\n### End Shapes\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `none` | No endpoint shape |\n| `arrow` | Arrow endpoint |\n\n## Colors\n\nThe `canvasColor` type can be specified in two ways:\n\n### Hex Colors\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": \"#FF0000\"\n}\n```\n\n### Preset Colors\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": \"1\"\n}\n```\n\n| Preset | Color |\n|--------|-------|\n| `\"1\"` | Red |\n| `\"2\"` | Orange |\n| `\"3\"` | Yellow |\n| `\"4\"` | Green |\n| `\"5\"` | Cyan |\n| `\"6\"` | Purple |\n\nNote: Specific color values for presets are intentionally undefined, allowing applications to use their own brand colors.\n\n## Complete Examples\n\n### Simple Canvas with Text and Connections\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"text\": \"# Main Idea\\n\\nThis is the central concept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": -100,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"text\": \"## Supporting Point A\\n\\nDetails here.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 100,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"text\": \"## Supporting Point B\\n\\nMore details.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Project Board with Groups\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"To Do\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 350,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"In Progress\",\n      \"color\": \"3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 700,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"Done\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 20,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 1\\n\\nImplement feature X\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 370,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 2\\n\\nReview PR #123\",\n      \"color\": \"2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 720,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 3\\n\\n~~Setup CI/CD~~\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n### Research Canvas with Files and Links\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 300,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 400,\n      \"height\": 200,\n      \"text\": \"# Research Topic\\n\\n## Key Questions\\n\\n- How does X affect Y?\\n- What are the implications?\",\n      \"color\": \"5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"file\": \"Literature/Paper A.pdf\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"file\": \"Notes/Meeting Notes.md\",\n      \"subpath\": \"#Key Insights\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c\",\n      \"type\": \"link\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 400,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"url\": \"https://example.com/research\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 750,\n      \"y\": 150,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 250,\n      \"file\": \"Attachments/diagram.png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"supports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"informs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toEnd\": \"arrow\",\n      \"color\": \"6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"visualized by\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Flowchart\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"**Start**\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 100,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Step 1:\\nGather data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"**Decision**\\n\\nIs data valid?\",\n      \"color\": \"3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Process data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Request new data\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 320,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"**End**\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"Yes\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toNode\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"toSide\": \"right\",\n      \"label\": \"No\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"top\",\n      \"fromEnd\": \"none\",\n      \"toNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toEnd\": \"arrow\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## ID Generation\n\nNode and edge IDs must be unique strings. Obsidian generates 16-character hexadecimal IDs:\n\n```json\n\"id\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\"\n\"id\": \"a3b2c1d0e9f8g7h6\"\n\"id\": \"1234567890abcdef\"\n```\n\nThis format is a 16-character lowercase hex string (64-bit random value).\n\n## Layout Guidelines\n\n### Positioning\n\n- Coordinates can be negative (canvas extends infinitely)\n- `x` increases to the right\n- `y` increases downward\n- Position refers to top-left corner of node\n\n### Recommended Sizes\n\n| Node Type | Suggested Width | Suggested Height |\n|-----------|-----------------|------------------|\n| Small text | 200-300 | 80-150 |\n| Medium text | 300-450 | 150-300 |\n| Large text | 400-600 | 300-500 |\n| File preview | 300-500 | 200-400 |\n| Link preview | 250-400 | 100-200 |\n| Group | Varies | Varies |\n\n### Spacing\n\n- Leave 20-50px padding inside groups\n- Space nodes 50-100px apart for readability\n- Align nodes to grid (multiples of 10 or 20) for cleaner layouts\n\n## Validation Rules\n\n1. All `id` values must be unique across nodes and edges\n2. `fromNode` and `toNode` must reference existing node IDs\n3. Required fields must be present for each node type\n4. `type` must be one of: `text`, `file`, `link`, `group`\n5. `backgroundStyle` must be one of: `cover`, `ratio`, `repeat`\n6. `fromSide`, `toSide` must be one of: `top`, `right`, `bottom`, `left`\n7. `fromEnd`, `toEnd` must be one of: `none`, `arrow`\n8. Color presets must be `\"1\"` through `\"6\"` or valid hex color\n\n## References\n\n- [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/)\n- [JSON Canvas GitHub](https://github.com/obsidianmd/jsoncanvas)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:52:33.342Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Visual Analysis Agents needing to create and edit infinite canvas data in JSON format.","zh":"非常适合需要创建和编辑无限画布数据以JSON格式的视觉分析代理。","ja":"Visual AnalysisエージェントがJSON形式で無限のキャンバスデータを作成および編集する必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"JSON 형식으로 무한 캔버스 데이터를 생성하고 편집해야 하는 시각적 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis Visual que necesitan crear y editar datos de lienzo infinito en formato JSON.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse Visuelle ayant besoin de créer et de modifier des données de canevas infini au format JSON.","de":"Perfekt für Visual Analysis Agents, die infinite Canvas-Daten im JSON-Format erstellen und bearbeiten müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Visual que precisam criar e editar dados de canvas infinito no formato JSON.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов визуального анализа, которым необходимо создавать и редактировать данные бесконечного холста в формате JSON.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل المرئي الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء وتحرير بيانات الشبكة غير المحدودة بتنسيق JSON."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and manipulate valid JSON Canvas files (.canvas) using the JSON Canvas Spec 1.0, enabling seamless integration with Obsidian and other compatible applications through Vue 3, Vite, and TypeScript.","zh":"赋予代理生成和操作符合JSON画布规范1.0的有效JSON画布文件(.canvas)，从而通过Vue 3、Vite和TypeScript实现与Obsidian和其他兼容应用程序的无缝集成。","ja":"JSON Canvas Spec 1.0に準拠した有効なJSON Canvasファイル(.canvas)を生成して操作するエージェントを可能にし、Vue 3、Vite、TypeScriptを通じてObsidianおよびその他の互換性のあるアプリケーションとのシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"JSON Canvas Spec 1.0에 맞는 유효한 JSON 캔버스 파일(.canvas)을 생성하고 조작할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, Vue 3, Vite 및 TypeScript를 통해 Obsidian 및 다른 호환되는 애플리케이션과 無縫な 통합을 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar y manipular archivos de lienzo JSON válidos (.canvas) utilizando la especificación JSON Canvas Spec 1.0, lo que permite una integración sin problemas con Obsidian y otras aplicaciones compatibles a través de Vue 3, Vite y TypeScript.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de manipuler des fichiers de canevas JSON valides (.canvas) en utilisant la spécification JSON Canvas Spec 1.0, permettant ainsi une intégration transparente avec Obsidian et d''autres applications compatibles via Vue 3, Vite et TypeScript.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, gültige JSON-Canvas-Dateien (.canvas) mithilfe der JSON Canvas Spec 1.0 zu generieren und zu manipulieren, was eine nahtlose Integration mit Obsidian und anderen kompatiblen Anwendungen über Vue 3, Vite und TypeScript ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e manipular arquivos de canvas JSON válidos (.canvas) usando a Especificação do Canvas JSON 1.0, permitindo integração perfeita com o Obsidian e outros aplicativos compatíveis por meio do Vue 3, Vite e TypeScript.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и манипулировать действительными файлами JSON Canvas (.canvas) с использованием Спецификации JSON Canvas 1.0, что обеспечивает беспрепятственную интеграцию с Obsidian и другими совместимыми приложениями посредством Vue 3, Vite и TypeScript.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على生成 وتعديل ملفات JSON Canvas صالحة (.canvas) باستخدام مواصفات JSON Canvas 1.0، مما يتيح التكامل السلس مع Obsidian وتطبيقات أخرى متوافقة من خلال Vue 3 و Vite و TypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating interactive node and edge networks","Editing existing .canvas files for Obsidian","Generating infinite canvas data for visualization"],"zh":["创建交互式节点和边网络","编辑现有的Obsidian用.canvas文件","生成无限画布数据用于可视化"],"ja":["相互作用するノードとエッジのネットワークを作成する","Obsidian用の既存の.canvasファイルを編集する","視覚化のために無限のキャンバスデータを生成する"],"ko":["상호 작용하는 노드와 에지 네트워크 생성","Obsidian용 기존 .canvas 파일 편집","시각화를 위한 무한 캔버스 데이터 생성"],"es":["Creación de redes interactivas de nodos y aristas","Edición de archivos .canvas existentes para Obsidian","Generación de datos de lienzo infinito para visualización"],"fr":["Création de réseaux de nœuds et d''arêtes interactifs","Édition de fichiers .canvas existants pour Obsidian","Génération de données de canevas infini pour visualisation"],"de":["Erstellung interaktiver Netzwerke aus Knoten und Kanten","Bearbeitung vorhandener .canvas-Dateien für Obsidian","Generierung von infiniten Canvas-Daten für Visualisierung"],"pt":["Criação de redes interativas de nodos e arestas","Edição de arquivos .canvas existentes para o Obsidian","Geração de dados de canvas infinito para visualização"],"ru":["Создание интерактивных сетей узлов и ребер","Редактирование существующих файлов .canvas для Obsidian","Генерация данных бесконечного холста для визуализации"],"ar":["إنشاء شبكات تفاعلية من العقد والحدود","تحرير ملفات .canvas الحالية لبرنامج Obsidian","генерация بيانات الشبكة غير المحدودة للتصوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires compatibility with JSON Canvas Spec 1.0","Limited to applications supporting .canvas files"],"zh":["需要与JSON画布规范1.0兼容","仅限支持.canvas文件的应用程序"],"ja":["JSON Canvas Spec 1.0との互換性が必要",".canvasファイルをサポートするアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["JSON Canvas Spec 1.0와의 호환성이 필요",".canvas 파일을 지원하는 애플리케이션으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con la especificación JSON Canvas Spec 1.0","Limitado a aplicaciones que admiten archivos .canvas"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec la spécification JSON Canvas Spec 1.0","Limité aux applications prenant en charge les fichiers .canvas"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit der JSON Canvas Spec 1.0","Begrenzt auf Anwendungen, die .canvas-Dateien unterstützen"],"pt":["Requer compatibilidade com a Especificação do Canvas JSON 1.0","Limitado a aplicações que suportam arquivos .canvas"],"ru":["Требует совместимости со Спецификацией JSON Canvas 1.0","Ограничен для приложений, поддерживающих файлы .canvas"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع مواصفات JSON Canvas 1.0","محدود للتطبيقات التي تدعم ملفات .canvas"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"174481b16ead9bfe7b417e59b14a952d72395fe04b31aa9e351d73d62f28fb90","qualityScore":31}');
